window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Hadley Hunter’s world is about to get bigger…and maybe not in a good way.<br> <br> When bodies wash up on the Moonstone Bay beach, it’s obvious there’s trouble afoot. Where, though? When her future mother-in-law identifies one of the bodies as belonging to Julian Nichols’ bodyguard, Hadley knows they’re in trouble.<br> <br> Julian Nichols is Miami’s biggest and baddest shifter…and he’s out there, somewhere. On top of that, come to find out, there’s some island gossip regarding Julian. It seems that his mother had an affair with Galen Blackwood’s father right around the time Julian was conceived. Does that mean Hadley’s fiancé has a brother? He doesn’t seem to think so. Hadley isn’t so certain, though.<br> <br> Finding Julian is of paramount importance. There’s just one little problem. The entire island is suddenly surrounded by sharks…and they’re of the aggressive variety.<br> <br> Nobody can get on or off Moonstone Bay. Someone is controlling the sharks and there are shifters lost at sea. What can they possibly do?<br> <br> It’s all hands on deck for another zany mystery. This one has teeth, however, and when the truth comes out at the end, nothing will ever be the same again.</p>"; 
